.TH SYNC 1 2026-09-25 "Substrate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sync \- flush file system buffers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sync
.RB [ \-d | \-\-data ]
.RB [ \-f | \-\-file\-system ]
.RB [ \-\- ]
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
With no
.I file
operands,
.B sync
calls
.BR sync (2)
to write all modified buffered data to storage.
.PP
With operands, each
.I file
is opened (read-only, or write-only if that fails, in both cases with
.BR O_NONBLOCK )
and flushed individually with
.BR fsync (2),
or
.BR fdatasync (2)
when
.B \-d
is given.
A file that cannot be opened or flushed is reported and the remaining
operands are still processed.
.PP
Option processing stops at the first argument that does not begin with
.BR \- ,
at a lone
.BR \- ,
or after
.BR \-\- .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-data
Use
.BR fdatasync (2)
instead of
.BR fsync (2).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file\-system
Accepted, but Substrate has no
.BR syncfs (2),
so each operand is simply flushed with
.BR fsync (2)
rather than flushing its whole file system.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage line and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.PP
If
.B \-d
or
.B \-f
is given without operands, a warning is printed and a global
.BR sync (2)
is performed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An invalid option was given, or at least one
.I file
could not be opened or flushed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fsync (2),
.BR fdatasync (2),
.BR sync (2)
